              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Input**\n\nI'm focusing on an ARC-like grid transformation task, specifically analyzing the provided training example. I've noted the 9x9 grid with a background of 8. I've begun to break down the input, identifying a few different colored L-trominoes within the grid. Now I am trying to determine a generalized concept to the L-trominoes' locations. I am focusing on their positions relative to their arrangement.\n\n\n**Identifying Corner Relationships**\n\nI've made a breakthrough. I've pinpointed the significance of the \"missing\" pixel in these shapes \u2013 the L-trominoes. Each color is a missing corner piece of a 2x2 square, forming a specific corner configuration: top-left, top-right, bottom-left, or bottom-right. The pattern now seems to map the missing corner to a specific corner of the output grid. I am now checking a second training case, focused on different colors, to validate this theory.\n\n\n**Validating Corner Mappings**\n\nI've tested my corner theory across several new cases. The bottom-left corner now shows shape X X, missing the bottom-right corner. The top-right now shows shape X X, missing the top-left corner. Additionally, the bottom-right shape is . X, missing the bottom-left corner. And the top-left missing the top-right! The output grid is divided into 4 quadrants, and the missing corner piece determines the value in each output quadrant.\n\n\n",
